From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: sunxi: A733 PF I/O voltage via PIN_CONFIG_POWER_SOURCE

License: GPL-2.0 (driver patch).

Implement the generic PIN_CONFIG_POWER_SOURCE pinconf for the A733
(sun60iw2) pinctrl so the SD/MMC UHS 1.8 V signalling switch needs no
variable vqmmc regulator. During UHS negotiation the mmc core calls
pinctrl_select_state() for the "mmc_1v8" state (1.8 V) or the default
(3.3 V); each state carries a power-source pinconf, and this new handler
writes the SoC PF-voltage register for it.

Mechanism and register
-----------------------
GPIO_POW_VAL_SET_CTL lives at pinctrl-base offset 0x0070 (a global PIO
register, not per-bank). bit 0 = VCC_PF_PWR_VOL_SEL, R/W, reset default
0x1. Encoding: 0 = 1.8 V, 1 = 3.3 V. Only bank PF is SoC-settable this
way.

  sunxi_pconf_set_power_source(): under pctl->lock, read the register and
  for arg == 1800000 CLEAR bit 0, else SET it. Note that the polarity is the
  opposite of the existing io-bias code (which uses uV<=1800000 ? 1 : 0) --
  here 1.8 V clears the bit. Gated on a new per-controller desc flag
  pf_power_switch (true only in a733_pinctrl_data) and on the pin being in
  bank PF (PF_BASE / PINS_PER_BANK), returning -ENOTSUPP otherwise, so every
  other SoC's desc and code path stays byte-identical.

  sunxi_pconf_set(): intercept PIN_CONFIG_POWER_SOURCE at the top of the
  per-config loop, before sunxi_pconf_reg() -- which returns -ENOTSUPP for
  this param and would otherwise abort. The argument contract is MICROVOLTS
  (1800000 / 3300000), matching the device tree power-source values (patch
  `arm64-dts-allwinner-a733-sd-uhs-sdr104`); a comment records the unit contract.

Evidence
--------
 - A733 user manual (offset 0x0070, GPIO_POW_VAL_SET_CTL, default
   0x00000001).
 - A733 UM v0.92, register table for GPIO_POW_VAL_SET_CTL: VCC_PF_PWR_VOL_SEL,
   0 = 1.8 V, 1 = 3.3 V.
 - Silicon readback on two 6 GiB boards, 2026-07-29: both boards read
   0x0070 = 0x0 while running SDR104 / 1.8 V signalling, i.e. bit 0 clear
   for 1.8 V, matching the encoding above.

Based on drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun55i-a523.c and the shared sunxi
core, Copyright (C) 2023 Arm Ltd.

The handler is reached through the DT power-source property, which sunxi's own
dt_node_to_map() and its config builder (drive-strength and bias only) do not
parse; is_generic = true does not route these nodes through the generic
parser. `pinctrl-sunxi-parse-the-generic-power-source-property` adds that
parsing and is what makes this handler reachable. A board test on 2026-07-29
saw GPIO_POW_VAL_SET_CTL still at its reset default for that reason; the
register, the polarity and the bank gate were not the cause.

HW effect pending: a green build only shows that it builds. The
polarity and the whole 1.8 V switch are unproven on silicon until a board
test on the 8 GiB board observes the SD card enumerating at SDR104 and 0x0070 reading
0x0 during 1.8 V signalling driven by our driver (not the boot chain).

Assisted-by: Claude
---
diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60iw2.c b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60iw2.c
index fe357b357..a8f673018 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60iw2.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60iw2.c
@@ -44,6 +44,12 @@ static const u8 a733_irq_bank_muxes[SUNXI_PINCTRL_MAX_BANKS] =
 	{  0, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14 };
 
 static struct sunxi_pinctrl_desc a733_pinctrl_data = {
+	/*
+	 * Bank PF I/O voltage is selected in the SoC via GPIO_POW_VAL_SET_CTL,
+	 * so the generic PIN_CONFIG_POWER_SOURCE handler can drive the SD UHS
+	 * 1.8 V signalling switch from the mmc_1v8 pinctrl state.
+	 */
+	.pf_power_switch = true,
 	.irq_banks = ARRAY_SIZE(a733_irq_bank_map),
 	.irq_bank_map = a733_irq_bank_map,
 	.irq_read_needs_mux = true,
diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c
index de3ee7a43..bce93c8e6 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c
@@ -653,6 +653,45 @@ static int sunxi_pconf_group_get(struct pinctrl_dev *pctldev,
 	return sunxi_pconf_get(pctldev, g->pin, config);
 }
 
+/*
+ * PIN_CONFIG_POWER_SOURCE for the bank PF I/O voltage (A733).
+ *
+ * The mmc core drives the SD UHS 1.8 V switch by selecting a pinctrl state
+ * whose power-source pinconf names the target signalling voltage; this handler
+ * writes the SoC PF-voltage bit for it (no variable vqmmc regulator needed).
+ *
+ * @pin is already pin_base-relative. Argument contract: MICROVOLTS
+ * (1800000 / 3300000), matching the device-tree power-source values.
+ *
+ * Register GPIO_POW_VAL_SET_CTL bit 0 = VCC_PF_PWR_VOL_SEL, 0 = 1.8 V /
+ * 1 = 3.3 V (A733 UM v0.92). Note that the polarity is the opposite of the io-bias
+ * code below: here 1.8 V clears bit 0.
+ */
+static int sunxi_pconf_set_power_source(struct sunxi_pinctrl *pctl,
+					unsigned pin, u32 arg)
+{
+	unsigned long flags;
+	u32 val;
+
+	if (!pctl->desc->pf_power_switch)
+		return -ENOTSUPP;
+
+	/* Only bank PF is SoC-settable through this register. */
+	if (pin / PINS_PER_BANK != PF_BASE / PINS_PER_BANK)
+		return -ENOTSUPP;
+
+	raw_spin_lock_irqsave(&pctl->lock, flags);
+	val = readl(pctl->membase + A733_POW_VAL_SET_CTL_REG);
+	if (arg == 1800000)
+		val &= ~BIT(0);
+	else
+		val |= BIT(0);
+	writel(val, pctl->membase + A733_POW_VAL_SET_CTL_REG);
+	raw_spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pctl->lock, flags);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int sunxi_pconf_set(struct pinctrl_dev *pctldev, unsigned pin,
 			   unsigned long *configs, unsigned num_configs)
 {
@@ -670,6 +709,19 @@ static int sunxi_pconf_set(struct pinctrl_dev *pctldev, unsigned pin,
 		param = pinconf_to_config_param(configs[i]);
 		arg = pinconf_to_config_argument(configs[i]);
 
+		/*
+		 * POWER_SOURCE (bank PF I/O voltage) is not a bank register the
+		 * way pull/drive are; sunxi_pconf_reg() returns -ENOTSUPP for it
+		 * and would abort the loop. Handle it here. Unit contract:
+		 * MICROVOLTS, same as the device-tree power-source value.
+		 */
+		if (param == PIN_CONFIG_POWER_SOURCE) {
+			ret = sunxi_pconf_set_power_source(pctl, pin, arg);
+			if (ret)
+				return ret;
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		ret = sunxi_pconf_reg(pctl, pin, param, &reg, &shift, &mask);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.h b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.h
index 5e7fb5501..8cdbe5606 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.h
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.h
@@ -69,6 +69,13 @@
 #define A733_IRQ_DEBOUNCE_REG		0xd8
 #define A733_IRQ_MEM_SIZE		0x80
 #define A733_POW_MOD_SEL_REG		0x40
+/*
+ * GPIO_POW_VAL_SET_CTL. bit 0 = VCC_PF_PWR_VOL_SEL: 0 = 1.8 V, 1 = 3.3 V,
+ * reset 0x1 (A733 UM v0.92). Global register (not per-bank); only
+ * bank PF is SoC-settable this way. Used by the PIN_CONFIG_POWER_SOURCE handler
+ * for the SD UHS 1.8 V signalling switch.
+ */
+#define A733_POW_VAL_SET_CTL_REG	0x70
 
 #define PINS_PER_BANK		32
 
@@ -161,6 +168,12 @@ struct sunxi_pinctrl_desc {
 	const unsigned int		*irq_bank_map;
 	bool				irq_read_needs_mux;
 	bool				disable_strict_mode;
+	/*
+	 * Set on SoCs whose bank PF I/O voltage is selected in the SoC itself
+	 * via GPIO_POW_VAL_SET_CTL (A733). Gates the PIN_CONFIG_POWER_SOURCE
+	 * handler so every other SoC's desc stays byte-identical.
+	 */
+	bool				pf_power_switch;
 	enum sunxi_desc_bias_voltage	io_bias_cfg_variant;
 	/*
 	 * IRQ register block. Zero keeps the classic layout (IRQ_CFG_REG and
